      "side": 1,
      "message": "In pKVM strict mode, domain_unmap() inside the pKVM hypervisor unconditionally flushes the hardware IOTLB on every single pkvm_domain_unmap() hypercall (called by iommu_unmap_fast()).\n\nAnd intel_iommu_tlb_sync() (called by iommu_iotlb_sync() at iommu_dma_unmap_batch_end()) is a no-op when pkvm_enabled() is true (if (!pkvm_enabled()) cache_tag_flush_range(...)).\n\nSo in pKVM mode, iommu_dma_unmap_batch_* doesn\u0027t save much. If 32 NVMe requests complete, pKVM still does 32 separate hypercalls and 32 separate QI IOTLB flushes.",
